From 68a2d319ee011550995ae9ee47bdf0b80c1d2771 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: James Dumay <jameswdumay@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 17:34:09 +1000
Subject: [PATCH] skippy: guard geometry annotation construction

Annotation sites in the architecture builders build a recipe on every graph
build, including an unsplit model's, and the result is dropped: only a capture
consumes one. Open the recipe as an intent record instead -- the site records
the axes it owns and skippy_stage_geometry_note() derives the rest from the
live tensor while the capture runs. Consumption that does not go through
note() (stage extraction fallbacks) derives immediately with
skippy_stage_geometry_snapshot(), and a recipe that is evaluated without being
derived fails closed instead of replaying a zeroed geometry.

skippy_stage_geometry_note_sites() and skippy_stage_geometry_recipe_derivations()
make the difference observable, and the structural coverage tests assert it: an
unsplit gemma build reaches 168 annotation sites and derives none, while the
same build under capture derives one recipe per site.
